es 179-198; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"8bea1785496c0dd5339551dbf462f8b3bc9c429aa73f39e50220b120fbacc655","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1989-12-28/pdf/FR-1989-12-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12698#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. U n ifo r m e d  S e r v ic e s . Pursuant to section 601 of Public Law 101-189, the  \nrates of monthly basic pay (37 U.S.C. 203(a)), the rates of basic allowances for  \nsubsistence (37 U.S.C. 402), and the rates of basic allowances for quarters (37  \nU.S.C. 403(a)) for members of the uniformed services are set forth at Schedules\n8- A and 8-B attached hereto and made a part hereof.\nSec.' 5. E ffe c t iv e  D a te s , (a) The rates of monthly basic pay and allowances for  \nsubsistence and quarters for members of the uniformed services provided for  \nat Schedule 8— A are effective on January 1, 1990. The rates of basic pay or  \nsalaries provided for at Schedules 1-A, 2, 3 -A  4, 5 -A  6-A, and 7-A are  \neffective on the first day of the first applicable pay period beginning on or  \nafter January 1,1990.\n(b) Pursuant to sections 702 and 1101 of Public Law 101-194 and section  \n11002(a)(3) of Public Law 101-239, the rates of monthly basic pay and allow­\nances for subsistence and quarters for members of the uniformed services  \nprovided for at Schedule 8-B shall supersede the rates provided for at  \nSchedule 8-A  on February 1, 1990, and the ratps of basic pay or salaries  \nprovided for at Schedules 1— B, 3— B, 5 — B , 6-B, and 7— B shall supersede the rates \nof basic pay or salaries provided for at Schedules 1-A, 3-A, 5-A, 6-A, and 7 -  \nA, respectively, effective on the first day of the first applicable pay period  \nbeginning on or after January 31,1990.\n\n=== PDF page 180 of 202 ===\n53474 Federal Register / Vol. 54, No. 248 / Thursday, December 28, 1989 /  Presidential Documents\nSec. 6. Executive Order No. 12663 of January 6,1989, is superseded.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"54 FR 53473, PDF pages 179-198; Sec. 4","sha256":"8bea1785496c0dd5339551dbf462f8b3bc9c429aa73f39e50220b120fbacc655","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1989-12-28/pdf/FR-1989-12-28.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12698#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":null,"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: original_representation not yet confirmed","DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 10 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)","CONFLICT NO_ORDER_CITED_IN_CURRENT_LAW: provisional NO, but 1 current-law predicate lead(s), e.g. CFR 29 CFR part 1471"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12698"}
